le for 16 dogs.\n   - Nate is responsible for 12 dogs.\n   - If Denali starts walking \\(4x\\) more dogs, her total number of dogs will be \\(16 + 4x\\).\n   - If \\(x\\) of Nate's dogs are reassigned to Denali, Denali's total number of dogs will be \\(16 + x\\) and Nate's total number of dogs will be \\(12 - x\\).\n\n2. **Setting up the Ratios:**\n   - The ratio of Denali's pay to Nate's pay when Denali walks \\(16 + 4x\\) dogs and Nate walks 12 dogs is \\(\\frac{16 + 4x}{12}\\).\n   - The ratio of Denali's pay to Nate's pay when \\(x\\) of Nate's dogs are reassigned to Denali is \\(\\frac{16 + x}{12 - x}\\).\n\n3. **Equating the Ratios:**\n   According to the problem, these two ratios are equal:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{16 + 4x}{12} = \\frac{16 + x}{12 - x}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Solving the Equation:**\n   Let's solve this equation step-by-step.\n\nFirst, we cross-multiply to eliminate the fractions:\n\\[\n(16 + 4x)(12 - x) = 12(16 + x)\n\\]\n\nExpanding both sides:\n\\[\n192 + 48x - 16x - 4x^2 = 192 + 12x\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the left side:\n\\[\n192 + 32x - 4x^2 = 192 + 12x\n\\]\n\nSubtract 192 from both sides:\n\\[\n32x - 4x^2 = 12x\n\\]\n\nRearrange the equation to set it to zero:\n\\[\n-4x^2 + 32x - 12x = 0\n\\]\n\nSimplify:\n\\[\n-4x^2 + 20x = 0\n\\]\n\nFactor out the greatest common factor:\n\\[\n-4x(x - 5) = 0\n\\]\n\nThis gives us two solutions:\n\\[\nx = 0 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x = 5\n\\]\n\nSince \\(x \\neq 0\\), the solution is \\(x = 5\\).\n\nLet's verify this solution using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\r\n\r\n# Define the variable\r\nx = symbols('x')\r\n\r\n# Define the equation based on the problem statement\r\nequation = Eq((16 + 4*x) / 12, (16 + x) / (12 - x))\r\n\r\n# Solve the equation\r\nsolution = solve(equation, x)\r\nprint(solution)\n```\n```output\n[0, 5]\n```\nThe solutions to the equation are \\(x = 0\\) and \\(x = 5\\). Since \\(x \\neq 0\\), the value of \\(x\\) is \\(\\boxed{5}\\).\n\nA company is l