:\n\\[i \\cdot (7 + 2i) = 7i + 2i^2 = 7i - 2 = -2 + 7i.\\]\n\n### Step 2: Translate the resulting complex number by \\(3 - 4i\\)\n\nAfter the rotation, we need to add \\(3 - 4i\\) to the resulting complex number \\(-2 + 7i\\):\n\\[-2 + 7i + 3 - 4i = (-2 + 3) + (7 - 4)i = 1 + 3i.\\]\n\nSo, the final complex number is \\(1 + 3i\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the initial complex number\nz = 7 + 2j\n\n# Rotate the complex number by 90 degrees counterclockwise (multiply by i)\nrotated_z = z * 1j\n\n# Translate the rotated complex number by 3 - 4i\nfinal_z = rotated_z + (3 - 4j)\n\nprint(final_z)\n```\n```output\n(1+3j)\n```\nThe final complex number after the rotation and translation is \\(\\boxed{1 + 3i}\\).", ' A $90^\\circ$ rotation around the origin in the counter-clockwise direction is applied to $7 + 2i.$  What is the resulting complex number?  (Express your answer in the form $a + bi.$)  \\boxed{The rotation of a complex number $z = a + bi$ by $90^\\circ$ counterclockwise around the origin can be represented by multiplying $z$ by $i$.  Therefore, the resulting complex number after the rotation is $i(7 + 2i) = -2 + 7i.$ \\boxed{-2 + 7i}', 'A $90^\\circ$ rotation around the origin in the counter-clockwise direction is applied to $7 + 2i.$  What is the resulting complex number? (Express your answer in the form $a + bi$.)\\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}