7:\n   - $4 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{7}$\n   - $6 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{7}$\n   - $8 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{7}$ (since $8 = 7 + 1$)\n5. So, $4 \\cdot 6 \\cdot 8 \\equiv 4 \\cdot 6 \\cdot 1 \\equiv 24 \\pmod{7}$.\n6. Now, we need to find the remainder when 24 is divided by 7. We can calculate this as follows: $24 = 3 \\cdot 7 + 3$, so $24 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{7}$.\n\nTherefore, the remainder when $(n + 2)(n + 4)(n + 6)$ is divided by 7 is 3.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given n ≡ 2 (mod 7), we substitute n with 2 in the expression (n + 2)(n + 4)(n + 6)\nn = 2\nexpression_value = (n + 2) * (n + 4) * (n + 6)\n\n# Find the remainder when the expression value is divided by 7\nremainder = expression_value % 7\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n3\n```\nThe remainder when $(n + 2)(n + 4)(n + 6)$ is divided by 7, given that $n \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7}$, is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).", 'Given the equation $x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0$, find the sum of the squares of its roots. \\boxed{}. \\quad \\text{(D) } 14 \\quad \\text{(E) } 16 \\quad \\text{(F) } 18 \\quad \\text{(G) } 20 \\quad \\text{(H) } 22 \\quad \\text{(I) } 24 \\quad \\text{(J) } 26 \\quad \\text{(K) } 28 \\quad \\text{(L) } 30 \\quad \\text{(M) } 32 \\quad \\text{(N) } 34 \\quad \\text{(O) } 36 \\quad \\text{(P) } 38 \\quad \\text{(Q) } 40 \\quad \\text{(R) } 42 \\quad \\text{(S) } 44 \\quad \\text{(T) } 46 \\quad \\text{(U) } 48 \\quad \\text{(V) } 50 \\quad \\text{(W) } 52 \\quad \\text{(X) } 54 \\quad \\text{(Y) } 56 \\quad \\text{(Z) } 58 \\quad \\text{(AA) } 60 \\quad \\text{(AB) } 62 \\quad \\text{(AC) } 64 \\quad \\text{(AD) } 66 \\quad \\text{(AE) } 68 \\quad \\text{(AF) } 70 \\quad \\text{(AG) } 72 \\quad \\text{(AH) } 74 \\quad \\text{(AI) } 76 \\quad \\text{(AJ) } 78 \\quad \\text{(AK) } 80 \\quad \\text{(AL) } 82 \\quad \\text{(AM) } 84 \\quad \\text{(AN) } 86 \\quad \\text{(AO) } 88 \\quad \\text{(AP) } 90 \\quad \\text{(AQ) } 92 \\quad \\text{(AR) } 94 \\quad \\text{(AS) } 96 \\quad \\text{(AT) } 98 \\