 components\ndef equation_solver():\n    # Assume x = 32\n    x = 32\n    \n    # Calculate the left side of the equation\n    log2_x2 = math.log2(x**2)\n    log_half_x = math.log2(x) / math.log2(1/2)\n    \n    # Sum of the two logarithmic terms\n    left_side = log2_x2 + log_half_x\n    \n    return left_side\n\n# Check if the left side equals 5 when x = 32\nresult = equation_solver()\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n5.0\n```\nThe Python code confirms that when \\( x = 32 \\), the left side of the equation \\(\\log_2 x^2 + \\log_{1/2} x\\) equals 5. Therefore, the solution to the equation is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{32}\n\\]\n\nGiven that the function $f(x)$ is an even function defined on $R$, and when $x \\geqslant 0$,", "To solve this problem, let's follow these steps:\n\n1. Define the side length of the original square.\n2. Calculate the new dimensions of the rectangle after the changes.\n3. Calculate the area of the original square and the new rectangle.\n4. Determine the percent decrease in area.\n\nLet's start by defining the side length of the original square as \\( s \\). The area of the original square is \\( s^2 \\).\n\nAfter the changes, the lengths of two opposite sides are decreased by 40%, so the new length of these sides is \\( 0.6s \\). The lengths of the other two sides are increased by 50%, so the new length of these sides is \\( 1.5s \\).\n\nThe area of the new rectangle is \\( 0.6s \\times 1.5s = 0.9s^2 \\).\n\nThe percent decrease in area is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Percent decrease} = \\left(1 - \\frac{\\text{New Area}}{\\text{Original Area}}\\right) \\times 100 = \\left(1 - \\frac{0.9s^2}{s^2}\\right) \\times 100 = (1 - 0.9) \\times 100 = 0.1 \\times 100 = 10\\%\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the side length of the original square\ns = 1  # The value of s does not matter as it will cancel out in the percentage calculation\n\n# Calculate the new dimensions of the rectangle\nnew_length_1 = 0.6 * s\nnew_length_2 = 1.5 