 n //= 9\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Convert 58_9 and 18_9 to base 10\nnum1_base_10 = 5 * 9 + 8\nnum2_base_10 = 1 * 9 + 8\n\n# Perform the subtraction in base 10\nresult_base_10 = num1_base_10 - num2_base_10\n\n# Convert the result back to base 9\nresult_base_9 = to_base_9(result_base_10)\nprint(result_base_9)\n```\n```output\n40\n```\nThe result of \\(58_9 - 18_9\\) in base 9 is \\(\\boxed{40_9}\\).', 'To solve the problem of subtracting $18_9$ from $58_9$ and expressing the answer in base $9$, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert both numbers from base $9$ to base $10$.\n2. Perform the subtraction in base $10$.\n3. Convert the result back to base $9$.\n\nLet\'s start by converting $58_9$ and $18_9$ to base $10$. The number $58_9$ can be expressed as:\n\\[5 \\cdot 9^1 + 8 \\cdot 9^0 = 5 \\cdot 9 + 8 \\cdot 1 = 45 + 8 = 53_{10}.\\]\nThe number $18_9$ can be expressed as:\n\\[1 \\cdot 9^1 + 8 \\cdot 9^0 = 1 \\cdot 9 + 8 \\cdot 1 = 9 + 8 = 17_{10}.\\]\n\nNext, we perform the subtraction in base $10$:\n\\[53_{10} - 17_{10} = 36_{10}.\\]\n\nFinally, we need to convert $36_{10}$ back to base $9$. To do this, we repeatedly divide the number by $9$ and keep track of the remainders.\n\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n&36 \\div 9 = 4 \\text{ remainder } 0, \\\\\n&4 \\div 9 = 0 \\text{ remainder } 4.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get $40_9$. Therefore, the final answer is:\n\\[58_9 - 18_9 = 40_9.\\]\n\nLet\'s verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Function to convert a base-10 number to base-9\ndef to_base_9(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    digits = []\n    while n:\n        digits.append(int(n % 9))\n        n //= 9\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Convert 58_9 and 18_9 to base-10\nnum1_base_10 = 5 * 9 + 8\nnum2_base_10 = 1 * 9 + 8\n\n# Perform the subtraction in base-10\nresult_base_10 = num1_base_10 - num2_base_10\n\n# Convert the result back to base-9\nresult_base_9 = to_base_9(result_base_10)\nprint(result_base_9)\n```\n```output\n40\n```\nThe result of $58_9 - 18_9$ is indeed $40_9$. Therefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{40_9}\n\\]', 'To solve the problem of subtracting \\(18_9\\) from \\(58_9\\) in base 9, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the base 9 numbers to base 10.\n2. Perform the subtraction in base 10.\n3. Convert the result back to base 9.\n\nLet\'s start by converting \\(58_9\\) and \\(18_9\\) to base 10. The general formula to convert a number from base \\(b\\) to base 10 is:\n\n\\[ \\text{number}_{10} = d_n \\cdot b^n + d_{n-1} \\cdot b^{n-1} + \\ldots + d_1 \\cdot b^1 + d_0 \\cdot b^0 \\]\n\nFor \\(58_9\\):\n\n\\[ 58_9 = 5 \\cdot 9^1 + 8 \\cdot 9^0 = 5 \\cdot 9 + 8 \\cdot 1 = 45 + 8 = 53_{10} \\]\n\nFor \\(18_9\\):\n\n\\[ 18_9 = 1 \\cdot 9^1 + 8 \\cdot 9^0 = 1 \\cdot 9 + 8 \\cdot 1 = 9 + 8 = 17_{10} \\]\n\nNow we perform the subtraction in base 10:\n\n\\[ 53_{10} - 17_{10} = 36_{10} \\]\n\nNext, we convert \\(36_{10}\\) back to base 9. To do this, we repeatedly divide the number by 9 and keep track of the remainders.\n\n\\[ 36 \\div 9 = 4 \\text{ remainder } 0 \\]\n\\[ 4 \\div 9 = 0 \\text{ remainder } 4 \\]\n\nReading the remainders from bottom to top, we get \\(40_9\\).\n\nSo, the final answer is \\(40_9\\).\n\nLet\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Function to convert a base 10 number to base 9\r\ndef to_base_9(n):\r\n    if n == 0:\r\n        return "0"\r\n    digits = []\r\n    while n:\r\n        digits.append(int(n % 9))\r\n        n //= 9\r\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\r\n\r\n# Convert 58_9 and 18_9 to base 10\r\nnum1_base_10 = 5 * 9 + 8\r\nnum2_base_10 = 1 * 9 + 8\r\n\r\n# Perform the subtraction in base 10\r\nresult_base_10 = num1_base_10 - num2_base_10\r\n\r\n# Convert the result back to base 9\r\nresult_base_9 = to_base_9(result_base_10)\r\nprint(result_base_9)\n```\n```output\n40\n```\nThe final answer, after performing the subtracti