: Multiply 10 by the reciprocal of 2/3\nreciprocal = Fraction(3, 2)\nresult2 = 10 * reciprocal\n\n# Problem 3: Find how much more sugar Polly needs\nsugar_needed = Fraction(2, 3)\nsugar_available = Fraction(1, 2)\nsugar_shortage = sugar_needed - sugar_available\n\nprint((result1, result2, sugar_shortage))\n```\n```output\n(Fraction(15, 1), Fraction(15, 1), Fraction(1, 6))\n```\nThe results from the Python code are as follows:\n\n1. \\(10 \\div \\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{15}{1} = 15\\)\n2. \\(10 \\times \\frac{3}{2} = \\frac{15}{1} = 15\\)\n3. \\(\\frac{2}{3} - \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{1}{6}\\)\n\nSo, the answers are:\n\n1. \\(10 \\div \\frac{2}{3} = \\boxed{15}\\)\n2. Polly needs to multiply 10 by \\(\\boxed{\\frac{3}{2}}\\) to get the answer.\n3. Polly needs \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{6}}\\) more cups of sugar.", 'The sum of two numbers is $10$ and their product is $24$.  What is the sum of the squares of these numbers?  (Express your answer in simplest form.)\\boxed{}.  (Express your answer in simplest form.)\\boxed{}.  (Express your answer in simplest form.)\\boxed{}.  (Express your answer in simplest form.)\\boxed{}.  (Express your answer in simplest form.)\\boxed{}.  (Express your answer in simplest form.)\\boxed{}.  (Express your answer in simplest form.)\\boxed{}.  (Express your answer in simplest form.)\\boxed{}.  (Express your answer in simplest form.)\\boxed{}.  (Express your answer in simplest form.)\\boxed{}.  (Express your answer in simplest form.)\\boxed{}.  (Express your answer in simplest form.)\\boxed{}.  (Express your answer in simplest form.)\\boxed{}.  (Express your answer in simplest form.)\\boxed{}.  (Express your answer in simplest form.)\\boxed{}.  (Express your answer in simplest form.)\\boxed{}.  (Express your answer in simplest form.)\\boxed{}.  (Express your answer in simplest form.)\\boxed{}.  (Express your answer in simplest form.)\\boxed{}.  (Express your answer in simplest form.)\\boxed{}.  (Express your answer in simplest form.)\\boxed{}.  (Expres