circ \\sin 50^\\circ$.\n   Using the identity $\\sin A \\cos B + \\cos A \\sin B = \\sin (A + B)$, we can rewrite the terms:\n   \\[\n   \\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ = \\sin (5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) = \\sin 25^\\circ\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   -\\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ = -(\\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ) = -\\sin (35^\\circ + 50^\\circ) = -\\sin 85^\\circ\n   \\]\n   So the denominator becomes:\n   \\[\n   \\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n3. **Combine the Simplified Numerator and Denominator:**\n   The expression for $\\tan \\theta$ now becomes:\n   \\[\n   \\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ}{\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ}\n   \\]\n   Using the sum-to-product identities, we have:\n   \\[\n   \\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ + 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ - 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos (-30^\\circ) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ + 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) \\sin \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ - 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin (-30^\\circ) = -2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ\n   \\]\n   So the expression for $\\tan \\theta$ becomes:\n   \\[\n   \\tan \\theta = \\frac{2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ}{-2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ} = \\frac{\\cos 30^\\circ}{-\\sin 30^\\circ} = -\\cot 30^\\circ = -\\sqrt{3}\n   \\]\n   Since $\\tan \\theta = -\\sqrt{3}$, the least positive angle $\\theta$ that satisfies this is $150^\\circ$ (since $\\tan 150^\\circ = -\\sqrt{3}$).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python and SymPy:\n\n```python\n", "To solve the given problem, we need to simplify the expression inside the tangent function and then find the angle $\\theta$ that satisfies the equation. Let's break down the problem step by step.\n\n1. **Simplify the numerator and 