etters of the word ELLIPSE? \\boxed{}.', 'Calculate the number of 7-digit telephone numbers that can be formed if the first digit cannot be 0 or 1 and no digit can appear more than once in the number. \\boxed{}.', 'Determine the number of ways to arrange the letters of the word TENNESSEE. \\boxed{2100}\n\nExplanation:\n\nTo calculate the number of ways to arrange the letters of a word with repeated letters, we use the formula:\n\n```\nn! / (n1! * n2! * ... * nk!)\n```\n\nwhere:\n\n* n is the total number of letters\n* n1, n2, ..., nk are the number of times each letter is repeated\n\nFor the word ELLIPSE:\n\n* n = 7\n* E is repeated 2 times\n* L is repeated 2 times\n\nTherefore, the number of ways to arrange the letters is:\n\n```\n7! / (2! * 2!) = 2100\n```\n\nFor the word TENNESSEE:\n\n* n = 8\n* T is repeated 2 times\n* E is repeated 4 times\n* N is repeated 2 times\n\nTherefore, the number of ways to arrange the letters is:\n\n```\n8! / (2! * 4! * 2!) = 2100\n```', 'How many ways can you arrange the letters of the word LOGIC if the letter C must always be first? \\boxed{}. Shayna is going to arrange her three colors of confetti (red, blue, and yellow) in a single row to decorate her birthday cake. How many ways can she arrange the confetti? Shayna is going to arrange her three colors of confetti (red, blue, and yellow) in a single row to decorate her birthday cake. How many ways can she arrange the confetti if she wants to have the blue and red next to each other? Shayna is going to arrange her three colors of confetti (red, blue, and yellow) in a single row to decorate her birthday cake. How many ways can she arrange the confetti if she wants to have the blue and red next to each other and the blue and yellow next to each other? Shayna is going to arrange her three colors of confetti (red, blue, and yellow) in a single row to decorate her birthday cake. How many ways can she arrange the confetti if she wants to have the blue and red next to each other and the b