xt{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| x_1y_2 + x_2y_3 + x_3y_4 + x_4y_1 - \\left( y_1x_2 + y_2x_3 + y_3x_4 + y_4x_1 \\right) \\right|\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the coordinates of \\(D(0, 3)\\), \\(B(0, 0)\\), \\(E(4, 0)\\), and \\(F\\left( \\frac{8}{3}, 2 \\right)\\) into the formula, we get:\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0 \\cdot 0 + 0 \\cdot 0 + 4 \\cdot 2 + \\frac{8}{3} \\cdot 3 - \\left( 3 \\cdot 0 + 0 \\cdot 4 + 0 \\cdot \\frac{8}{3} + 2 \\cdot 0 \\right) \\right|\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0 + 0 + 8 + 8 - (0 + 0 + 0 + 0) \\right|\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 16 \\right|\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 16\n\\]\n\\[\n= 8\n\\]\n\nSo, the area of quadrilateral \\(DBEF\\) is \\(\\boxed{8}\\).", "To determine the area of quadrilateral \\(DBEF\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the coordinates of points \\(D\\) and \\(E\\).\n2. Use the coordinates of points \\(D\\), \\(B\\), \\(E\\), and \\(F\\) to calculate the area of quadrilateral \\(DBEF\\).\n\nFirst, let's identify the coordinates of points \\(D\\) and \\(E\\):\n\n- \\(D\\) is the midpoint of \\(\\overline{AB}\\). The coordinates of \\(D\\) are \\(\\left( \\frac{0+0}{2}, \\frac{6+0}{2} \\right) = (0, 3)\\).\n- \\(E\\) is the midpoint of \\(\\overline{BC}\\). The coordinates of \\(E\\) are \\(\\left( \\frac{0+8}{2}, \\frac{0+0}{2} \\right) = (4, 0)\\).\n\nNext, we need the coordinates of point \\(F\\). Since \\(F\\) is the intersection of \\(\\overline{AE}\\) and \\(\\overline{CD}\\), we need to find the equations of lines \\(AE\\) and \\(CD\\) and solve for their intersection.\n\nThe equation of line \\(AE\\) can be determined using the points \\(A(0, 6)\\) and \\(E(4, 0)\\):\n- The slope of \\(AE\\) is \\(\\frac{0-6}{4-0} = -\\frac{3}{2}\\).\n- The equation of the line in point-slope form is \\(y - 6 = -\\frac{3}{2}(x - 0)\\), which simplifies to \\(y = -\\frac{3}{2}x + 6\\).\n\nThe equation of line \\(CD\\) can be determined using the points \\(C(8, 0)\\) and \\(D(0, 3)\\):\n- The slope of \\(CD\\) is \\(\\frac{3-0}{0-8} = -\\frac{3}{8}\\).\n- The equation of the line in point-slope form is \\(y - 0 = -\\frac{3}{8}(x - 8)\\), which simplifies to \\(y = -\\frac{3}{8}x + 3\\).\n\nTo find the intersection of these two lines, we set the equations equal to each other:\n\\[ -\\frac{3}{2}x + 6 = -\\frac{3}{8}x + 3 \\]\nMultiplying through by 8 to clear the fractions:\n\\[ -12x + 48 = -3x + 24 \\]\nRearranging terms:\n\\[ -9x = -24 \\]\nSo, \\(x = \\frac{24}{9} = \\frac{8}{3}\\).\nSubstituting \\(x = \\frac{8}{3}\\) back into the equation \\(y = -\\frac{3}{2}x + 6\\):\n\\[ y = -\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\frac{8}{3}\\right) + 6 = -4 + 6 = 2 \\]\nSo, the coordinates of \\(F\\) are \\(\\left( \\frac{8}{3}, 2 \\right)\\).\n\nNow we have the coordinates of points \\(D(0, 3)\\), \\(B(0, 0)\\), \\(E(4, 0)\\), and \\(F\\left( \\frac{8}{3}, 2 \\right)\\). We can use the shoelace formula to find the area of quadrilateral \\(DBEF\\):\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| x_1y_2 + x_2y_3 + x_3y_4 + x_4y_1 - (y_1x_2 + y_2x_3 + y_3x_4 + y_4x_1) \\right| \\]\nSubstituting in the coordinates:\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0 \\cdot 0 + 0 \\cdot 0 + 4 \\cdot 2 + \\frac{8}{3} \\cdot 3 - (3 \\cdot 0 + 0 \\cdot 4 + 0 \\cdot \\frac{8}{3} + 2 \\cdot 0) \\right| \\]\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0 + 0 + 8 + 8 - (0 + 0 + 0 + 0) \\right| \\]\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 16 \\right| = 8 \\]\n\nSo, the area of quadrilateral \\(", "To determine the area of quadrilateral $DBEF$, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the coordinates of points $D$ and $E$.\n2. Use the coordinates of points $D$, $B$, $E$, and $F$ to calculate the area of quadrilateral $DBEF$ using the Shoelace formula.\n\nLet's start by identifying the coordinates of points $D$ and $E$:\n\n- $D$ is the midpoint of $\\overline{AB}$, so its coordinates are $\\left(\\frac{0+0}{2}, \\frac{6+0}{2}\\right) = (0, 3)$.\n- $E$ is the midpoint of $\\overline{BC}$, so its coordinates are $\\