\'x\')\n\n# Define the equation |x+5| = |3x-6|\nequation1 = sp.Eq(x + 5, 3*x - 6)\nequation2 = sp.Eq(x + 5, -(3*x - 6))\n\n# Solve the equations\nsolution1 = sp.solve(equation1, x)\nsolution2 = sp.solve(equation2, x)\n\n# Combine the solutions and find the maximum value\nsolutions = solution1 + solution2\nmax_solution = max(solutions)\n\nprint(max_solution)\n```\n```output\n11/2\n```\nThe largest possible value of \\(x\\) that satisfies the equation \\(|x+5|-|3x-6|=0\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{11}{2}}\\).', 'Evaluate $\\lceil (3.4)^2 \\rceil + ( \\lceil 3.4 \\rceil ) ^2$. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{}. \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\boxed{} \\