o ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the equation components\nnumerator1 = 2\ndenominator1 = 3\nnumerator2 = 4\ndenominator2 = 11 - 5\n\n# Check if the equation holds true\nleft_side = numerator1 / denominator1\nright_side = numerator2 / denominator2\n\n# Verify the solution\nprint((left_side, right_side, left_side == right_side))\n```\n```output\n(0.6666666666666666, 0.6666666666666666, True)\n```\nThe left side of the equation \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\) and the right side of the equation \\(\\frac{4}{11-5} = \\frac{4}{6} = \\frac{2}{3}\\) both evaluate to approximately 0.6667, confirming that the solution \\(x = 11\\) is correct.\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{11}\n\\]", 'To solve the equation \\(\\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{4}{x-5}\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Cross-multiply to eliminate the fractions:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{4}{x-5}\n   \\]\n   Cross-multiplying gives:\n   \\[\n   2 \\cdot (x - 5) = 3 \\cdot 4\n   \\]\n\n2. **Simplify the equation:**\n   \\[\n   2(x - 5) = 12\n   \\]\n\n3. **Distribute the 2 on the left-hand side:**\n   \\[\n   2x - 10 = 12\n   \\]\n\n4. **Isolate the term with \\(x\\) by adding 10 to both sides:**\n   \\[\n   2x - 10 + 10 = 12 + 10\n   \\]\n   Simplifying this, we get:\n   \\[\n   2x = 22\n   \\]\n\n5. **Solve for \\(x\\) by dividing both sides by 2:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2x}{2} = \\frac{22}{2}\n   \\]\n   Simplifying this, we get:\n   \\[\n   x = 11\n   \\]\n\n6. **Verify the solution by substituting \\(x = 11\\) back into the original equation:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{4}{11-5}\n   \\]\n   Simplifying the right-hand side:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{4}{6}\n   \\]\n   Simplifying \\(\\frac{4}{6}\\) to \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{2}{3}\n   \\]\n   The equation holds true, confirming our solution.\n\nTherefore, the solution to the equation is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{11}\n\\]', "To solve this problem, we need to find a number \\( x \\) that satisfies the following condition