refore, \\( \\angle BAC = \\frac{900^\\circ}{7} - 90^\\circ = \\frac{900^\\circ - 630^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{270^\\circ}{7} \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python and sympy:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the internal angle of the heptagon and the square\ninternal_angle_heptagon = sp.Rational(900, 7)\ninternal_angle_square = 90\n\n# Calculate the angle BAC\nangle_BAC = internal_angle_heptagon - internal_angle_square\nangle_BAC = sp.simplify(angle_BAC)\n\nprint(angle_BAC)\n```\n```output\n270/7\n```\nThe degree measure of angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{270}{7}}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to determine the measure of angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) where \\( \\angle BAD \\) is an interior angle of a regular heptagon and \\( \\angle CAD \\) is a right angle (90 degrees) because \\( \\overline{AD} \\) is a side of a square.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the measure of each interior angle of a regular heptagon. The formula for the measure of an interior angle of a regular polygon with \\( n \\) sides is:\n\\[\n\\text{Interior angle} = \\frac{(n-2) \\cdot 180^\\circ}{n}\n\\]\nFor a heptagon (\\( n = 7 \\)):\n\\[\n\\text{Interior angle of heptagon} = \\frac{(7-2) \\cdot 180^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{5 \\cdot 180^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{900^\\circ}{7}\n\\]\nSo, \\( \\angle BAD = \\frac{900^\\circ}{7} \\).\n\nSince \\( \\overline{AD} \\) is a side of a square, \\( \\angle CAD = 90^\\circ \\).\n\nThe angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) is the difference between \\( \\angle BAD \\) and \\( \\angle CAD \\):\n\\[\n\\angle BAC = \\angle BAD - \\angle CAD = \\frac{900^\\circ}{7} - 90^\\circ\n\\]\nTo perform the subtraction, we need a common denominator:\n\\[\n90^\\circ = \\frac{630^\\circ}{7}\n\\]\nSo:\n\\[\n\\angle BAC = \\frac{900^\\circ}{7} - \\frac{630^\\circ}{7} = \\frac{270^\\circ}{7}\n\\]\nThus, the degree measure of angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) is \\( \\frac{270^\\circ}{7} \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure the calculation is accurate.\n```python\n# C