 to find the smallest possible value of \\(|m - n|\\) given the equation \\(3m + 4n = 100\\). Here's the step-by-step approach:\n\n1. **Express \\(m\\) in terms of \\(n\\):**\n   \\[\n   3m = 100 - 4n \\implies m = \\frac{100 - 4n}{3}\n   \\]\n   For \\(m\\) to be an integer, \\(100 - 4n\\) must be divisible by 3. This means \\(100 - 4n \\equiv 0 \\pmod{3}\\), or \\(4n \\equiv 100 \\pmod{3}\\). Since \\(4 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}\\) and \\(100 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}\\), we get \\(n \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}\\). So \\(n\\) can be written as \\(n = 3k + 1\\) for some integer \\(k\\).\n\n2. **Substitute \\(n = 3k + 1\\) into the equation for \\(m\\):**\n   \\[\n   m = \\frac{100 - 4(3k + 1)}{3} = \\frac{100 - 12k - 4}{3} = \\frac{96 - 12k}{3} = 32 - 4k\n   \\]\n   So we have \\(m = 32 - 4k\\) and \\(n = 3k + 1\\).\n\n3. **Find the expression for \\(|m - n|\\):**\n   \\[\n   |m - n| = |(32 - 4k) - (3k + 1)| = |31 - 7k|\n   \\]\n   We need to find the integer \\(k\\) that minimizes \\(|31 - 7k|\\).\n\n4. **Determine the value of \\(k\\) that minimizes \\(|31 - 7k|\\):**\n   The expression \\(|31 - 7k|\\) will be minimized when \\(7k\\) is as close as possible to 31. The closest multiple of 7 to 31 is 28 (since \\(7 \\times 4 = 28\\)). So \\(k = 4\\) is a good candidate.\n\n5. **Verify the value of \\(k = 4\\):**\n   \\[\n   k = 4 \\implies m = 32 - 4 \\cdot 4 = 16 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad n = 3 \\cdot 4 + 1 = 13\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   |m - n| = |16 - 13| = 3\n   \\]\n   We should check if there are any smaller values by considering \\(k = 3\\) and \\(k = 5\\):\n   \\[\n   k = 3 \\implies m = 32 - 4 \\cdot 3 = 20 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad n = 3 \\cdot 3 + 1 = 10 \\implies |m - n| = |20 - 10| = 10\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   k = 5 \\implies m = 32 - 4 \\cdot 5 = 12 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad n = 3 \\cdot 5 + 1 = 16 \\implies |m - n| = |12 - 16| = 4\n   \\]\n   The smallest value we found is \\(|m - n| = 3\\) when \\(k = 4\\).\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of \\(|m - n|\\) is \\(\\boxed