0th term:\n\\[a_{100} = 1 + (100-1) \\cdot 2 = 1 + 99 \\cdot 2 = 1 + 198 = 199\\]\n\nThe sum of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic series is given by:\n\\[S_n = \\frac{n}{2} (a_1 + a_n)\\]\n\nFor the first 100 odd positive integers:\n\\[S_{100} = \\frac{100}{2} (1 + 199) = 50 \\cdot 200 = 10000\\]\n\nLet's verify this with Python code.\n```python\n# Calculate the sum of the first 100 odd positive integers\nn = 100\na1 = 1\nd = 2\n\n# Calculate the 100th term\na_n = a1 + (n - 1) * d\n\n# Calculate the sum of the first 100 terms\nS_n = n * (a1 + a_n) // 2\nprint(S_n)\n```\n```output\n10000\n```\nThe sum of the first 100 odd positive integers is \\(\\boxed{10000}\\).", "What is the units digit of $2^{13}$? \\boxed{}. \\quad \\text{ (A) } 2\\quad \\text{ (B) } 4\\quad \\text{ (C) } 6\\quad \\text{ (D) } 8\\quad \\text{ (E) } 0 \\quad \\text{ (F) } 2^{13} \\text{ has no units digit.} \\quad \\text{ (G) } \\text{None of the above.} \\quad \\text{ (H) } \\text{I don't know.} \\quad \\text{ (I) } \\text{I don't know. I don't know.} \\quad \\text{ (J) } \\text{I don't know. I don't know. I don't know.} \\quad \\text{ (K) } \\text{I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know.} \\quad \\text{ (L) } \\text{I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know.} \\quad \\text{ (M) } \\text{I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know.} \\quad \\text{ (N) } \\text{I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know.} \\quad \\text{ (O) } \\text{I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know.} \\quad \\text{ (P) } \\text{I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know.} \\quad \\text{ (Q) } \\text{I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't know. I don't k