ute p(3) and p(4)\np3 = p.subs(x, 3)\np4 = p.subs(x, 4)\n\n# Calculate the ratio p(3) / p(4)\nratio = p3 / p4\n\n# Print the ratio\nprint(ratio)\n```\n```output\n14\n```\nThe ratio \\(\\frac{p(3)}{p(4)}\\) for the quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients that has \\(4 - \\sqrt{11}\\) as a root is \\(\\boxed{14}\\).", 'Let $p(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $4-\\sqrt{11}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{p(3)}{p(4)}.$\nLet $p(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $4-\\sqrt{11}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{p(3)}{p(4)}.$\nLet $p(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $4-\\sqrt{11}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{p(3)}{p(4)}.$\nLet $p(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $4-\\sqrt{11}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{p(3)}{p(4)}.$\nLet $p(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $4-\\sqrt{11}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{p(3)}{p(4)}.$\nLet $p(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $4-\\sqrt{11}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{p(3)}{p(4)}.$\nLet $p(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $4-\\sqrt{11}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{p(3)}{p(4)}.$\nLet $p(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $4-\\sqrt{11}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{p(3)}{p(4)}.$\nLet $p(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $4-\\sqrt{11}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{p(3)}{p(4)}.$\nLet $p(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $4-\\sqrt{11}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{p(3)}{p(4)}.$\nLet $p(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $4-\\sqrt{11}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{p(3)}{p(4)}.$\nLet $p(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $4-\\sqrt{11}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{p(3)}{p(4)}.$\nLet $p(x)$ be a quadratic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $4-\\sqrt{11}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac