$P(x)$ are three distinct positive integers. If $P(0) = 30$, compute the largest possible value of $P(7).$ 2022 CCA Math Bonanza Lightning Round #2.1\nTo solve the problem, we need to find the quadratic polynomial \\( p(x) \\) with integer coefficients that has \\( 4 - \\sqrt{11} \\) as a root. Since the coefficients are integers, the conjugate \\( 4 + \\sqrt{11} \\) must also be a root. Therefore, the quadratic polynomial can be written as:\n\n\\[ p(x) = (x - (4 - \\sqrt{11}))(x - (4 + \\sqrt{11})) \\]\n\nExpanding this, we get:\n\n\\[ p(x) = (x - 4 + \\sqrt{11})(x - 4 - \\sqrt{11}) = (x - 4)^2 - (\\sqrt{11})^2 = x^2 - 8x + 16 - 11 = x^2 - 8x + 5 \\]\n\nNow, we need to compute \\( \\frac{p(3)}{p(4)} \\):\n\n\\[ p(3) = 3^2 - 8 \\cdot 3 + 5 = 9 - 24 + 5 = -10 \\]\n\\[ p(4) = 4^2 - 8 \\cdot 4 + 5 = 16 - 32 + 5 = -11 \\]\n\nSo, \\( \\frac{p(3)}{p(4)} = \\frac{-10}{-11} = \\frac{10}{11} \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the polynomial function p(x) = x^2 - 8x + 5\ndef p(x):\n    return x**2 - 8*x + 5\n\n# Compute p(3) and p(4)\np_3 = p(3)\np_4 = p(4)\n\n# Compute the ratio p(3) / p(4)\nratio = p_3 / p_4\nprint(ratio)\n```\n```output\n0.9090909090909091\n```\nThe ratio \\(\\frac{p(3)}{p(4)}\\) is \\(\\frac{10}{11}\\), which is approximately 0.9090909090909091 when computed.\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{10}{11}}\n\\]", 'Let $p(x)$ be a cubic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $1+\\sqrt{2}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{p(3)}{p(4)}.$ 2023 AIME I #11\nLet $p(x)$ be a cubic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $1+\\sqrt{2}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{p(3)}{p(4)}.$ 2023 AIME I #11\nLet $p(x)$ be a cubic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $1+\\sqrt{2}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{p(3)}{p(4)}.$ 2023 AIME I #11\nLet $p(x)$ be a cubic polynomial with integer coefficients which has $1+\\sqrt{2}$ as a root. Compute $\\frac{p(3)}{p(4)}.$ 2023 AIME I #11\nLet $p(x)$ be a cubic polynomial with integer 