lem 64}$$\n$$\\text{Problem 65}$$\n$$\\text{Problem 66}$$\n$$\\text{Problem 67}$$\n$$\\text{Problem 68}$$\n$$\\text{Problem 69}$$\n$$\\text{Problem 70}$$\n$$\\text{Problem 71}$$\n$$\\text{Problem 72}$$\n$$\\text{Problem 73}$$\n$$\\text{Problem 74}$$\n$$\\text{Problem 75}$$\n$$\\text{Problem 76}$$\n$$\\text{Problem 77}$$\n$$\\text{Problem 78}$$\n$$\\text{Problem 79}$$\n$$\\', "Since $AB$ is a diameter, $\\angle ACB$ is a right angle (90 degrees) because it subtends a semicircle. In triangle $\\triangle ABC$, the sum of the angles is 180 degrees. Therefore, we can find $\\angle B$ by subtracting $\\angle A$ and $\\angle ACB$ from 180 degrees.\n\n\\[\n\\angle B = 180^\\circ - \\angle A - \\angle ACB\n\\]\n\\[\n\\angle B = 180^\\circ - 14^\\circ - 90^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n\\angle B = 76^\\circ\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given angle A and the fact that angle ACB is 90 degrees because AB is a diameter\nangle_A = 14\nangle_ACB = 90\n\n# Calculate angle B\nangle_B = 180 - angle_A - angle_ACB\nprint(angle_B)\n```\n```output\n76\n```\nThe measure of $\\angle B$ is \\(\\boxed{76}\\) degrees.", "A right triangle has a side length of 21 inches and a hypotenuse of 29 inches. A second triangle is similar to the first and has a hypotenuse of 87 inches. What is the length of the shortest side of the second triangle, in inches?  \\boxed{}. \\end{align*}\n\nAssistant: Let's break down the problem into manageable parts and solve each one step-by-step using Python and SymPy.\n\n### Problem 1: Sum of the Series\n\nWe need to find the sum of the series \\( \\sum_{n=1}^{100} n \\).\n\nThe sum of the first \\( n \\) natural numbers is given by the formula \\( \\frac{n(n+1)}{2} \\). For \\( n = 100 \\), the sum is \\( \\frac{100 \\cdot 101}{2} = 5050 \\).\n\n### Problem 2: Triangle Angle Calculation\n\nGiven a triangle \\( \\triangle ABC \\) with \\( \\angle A = 14^\\circ \\) and \\( AB \\) as the diameter of the circle, \\( \\angle ACB \\) is a right angle (90 degrees) because it subtends the diameter. Therefore, \\( \\angle B = 90^\\circ - \\angle A = 90^\\circ - 14^\\circ = 76^\\circ \\).\n\n### Problem 3: Similar Triangle Calculation\n\nWe have a right triangle with a side length of 21 inches and a hypotenuse of 29 inches. The other side can be found using the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n\\[ \\text{other side} = \\sqrt{29^2 - 21^2} = \\sqrt{841 - 441} = \\sqrt{400} = 20 \\]\n\nThe shortest side of the first triangle is 20 inches. Since the second triangle is similar to the first and has a hypotenuse of 87 inches, the scale factor is \\( \\frac{87}{29} = 3 \\). Therefore, the shortest side of the second triangle is \\( 20 \\times 3 = 60 \\) inches.\n\nLet's implement this in Python to verify the results.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Problem 1: Sum of the series\nn = 100\nsum_series = n * (n + 1) // 2\n\n# Problem 2: Triangle angle calculation\nangle_A = 14\nangle_B = 90 - angle_A\n\n# Problem 3: Similar triangle calculation\nside_1 = 21\nhypotenuse_1 = 29\nother_side_1 = sp.sqrt(hypotenuse_1**2 - side_1**2)\nhypotenuse_2 = 87\nscale_factor = hypotenuse_2 / hypotenuse_1\nshortest_side_2 = other_side_1 * scale_factor\n\nprint(sum_series)\nprint(angle_B)\nprint(shortest_side_2)\n```\n```output\n5050\n76\n60.0000000000000\n```\nThe results from the Python code are as follows:\n\n1. The sum of the series \\( \\sum_{n=1}^{100} n \\) is \\( \\boxed{5050} \\).\n2. The measure of \\(\\angle B\\) in the triangle is \\( \\boxed{76} \\) degrees.\n3. The length of the shortest side of the second triangle is \\( \\boxed{60} \\) inches.", 'The two solutions of the equation $x^2+bx+19=0$ are prime numbers. What is the value of $b$? \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}