\circ\n   \\]\n\n2. Finding $\\angle B$ in $\\triangle ABC$:\n\n   Since $AB$ is a diameter, $\\angle ACB$ is a right angle (Inscribed Angle Theorem). Thus, $\\angle ACB = 90^\\circ$.\n\n   Given $\\angle A = 14^\\circ$, we can find $\\angle B$ using the fact that the sum of angles in a triangle is $180^\\circ$:\n   \\[\n   \\angle B = 180^\\circ - \\angle A - \\angle ACB = 180^\\circ - 14^\\circ - 90^\\circ = 76^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n3. Finding $\\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y}$:\n\n   Given $2^x = 10$ and $5^y = 10$, we need to express $10$ in terms of powers of $2$ and $5$:\n   \\[\n   10 = 2^1 \\cdot 5^1\n   \\]\n\n   Therefore, $x = 1$ and $y = 1$. Now, we find $\\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y}$:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y} = \\frac{1}{1} + \\frac{1}{1} = 1 + 1 = 2\n   \\]\n\n### Final Answers:\n- For the quadrilateral $ABCD$, the angles are:\n  \\[\n  \\angle A = 14^\\circ, \\angle B = 90^\\circ, \\angle C = 90^\\circ, \\angle D = 90^\\circ\n  \\]\n- For $\\triangle ABC$, $\\angle B = 76^\\circ$.\n- $\\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y} = 2$.', 'The value of a painting increases by 10% every year. A particular painting\nwas worth $200 in 2013. How much was it worth in 2008? \\boxed{}. \\textbf{Calculator allowed}\n\\textit{Assistant}\nA triangle $\\triangle ABC$ with $\\angle A = 14^\\circ$ is inscribed in a circle where $AB$ is a diameter. How many degrees are in $\\angle B$? \\boxed{}. \\textbf{Calculator allowed}\n\\textit{Assistant}\nThe value of a painting increases by 10% every year. A particular painting\nwas worth $200 in 2013. How much was it worth in 2008? \\boxed{}. \\textbf{Calculator allowed}\n\\textit{Assistant}\nA triangle $\\triangle ABC$ with $\\angle A = 14^\\circ$ is inscribed in a circle where $AB$ is a diameter. How many degrees are in $\\angle B$? \\boxed{}. \\textbf{Calculator allowed}\n\\textit{Assistant}\nThe value of a painting increases by 10% every year. A particular painting\nwas worth $200 in 2013. How much was it worth in 2008? \\boxed{}. \