n find the remainder when this sum is divided by 9. The formula for the sum of the first \\(n\\) natural numbers is:\n\n\\[ S = \\frac{n(n+1)}{2} \\]\n\nFor the first problem, \\(n = 10\\):\n\n\\[ S_{10} = \\frac{10 \\times 11}{2} = 55 \\]\n\nFor the second problem, \\(n = 11\\):\n\n\\[ S_{11} = \\frac{11 \\times 12}{2} = 66 \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainders when 55 and 66 are divided by 9. We can use Python to perform these calculations accurately.\n```python\n# Calculate the sums\nsum_10 = 10 * 11 // 2\nsum_11 = 11 * 12 // 2\n\n# Calculate the remainders when divided by 9\nremainder_10 = sum_10 % 9\nremainder_11 = sum_11 % 9\n\nprint((sum_10, remainder_10, sum_11, remainder_11))\n```\n```output\n(55, 1, 66, 3)\n```\nThe sum of the first 10 natural numbers is 55, and the remainder when 55 is divided by 9 is 1.\n\nThe sum of the first 11 natural numbers is 66, and the remainder when 66 is divided by 9 is 3.\n\nSo, the final answers are:\n\n1. The remainder when \\(1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + \\dots + 9 + 10\\) is divided by 9 is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).\n2. The remainder when \\(1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + \\dots + 9 + 10 + 11\\) is divided by 9 is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).', "What is the remainder when $1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + \\dots + 9 + 10 + 11$ is divided by 9? Shay\n1. Calculate the sum of the first 10 natural numbers and find the remainder when divided by 9.\n2. Calculate the sum of the first 11 natural numbers and find the remainder when divided by 9.\nTo solve these problems, we'll use the formula for the sum of the first \\( n \\) natural numbers:\n\n$$\nS_n = \\frac{n(n+1)}{2}\n$$\n\nwhere \\( S_n \\) is the sum of the first \\( n \\) natural numbers.\n\n#### Part 1: Sum of the first 10 natural numbers\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the first 10 natural numbers:\n\n$$\nS_{10} = \\frac{10 \\times (10+1)}{2} = \\frac{10 \\times 11}{2} = 55\n$$\n\nNext, we find the remainder when 55 is divided by 9:\n\n$$\n55 \\div 9 = 6 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\; 1\n$$\n\nSo, the remainder when the sum of 