} + \\frac{1}{c} + \\frac{1}{d} \\right)\\), we can use the method of mathematical reasoning and the AM-HM (Arithmetic Mean-Harmonic Mean) inequality.\n\nThe AM-HM inequality states that for any set of positive real numbers \\(x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n\\),\n\\[\n\\frac{x_1 + x_2 + \\cdots + x_n}{n} \\geq \\frac{n}{\\frac{1}{x_1} + \\frac{1}{x_2} + \\cdots + \\frac{1}{x_n}}\n\\]\nwith equality if and only if \\(x_1 = x_2 = \\cdots = x_n\\).\n\nFor \\(a, b, c, d\\), the AM-HM inequality gives us:\n\\[\n\\frac{a + b + c + d}{4} \\geq \\frac{4}{\\frac{1}{a} + \\frac{1}{b} + \\frac{1}{c} + \\frac{1}{d}}\n\\]\nRearranging this inequality, we get:\n\\[\n(a + b + c + d) \\left( \\frac{1}{a} + \\frac{1}{b} + \\frac{1}{c} + \\frac{1}{d} \\right) \\geq 16\n\\]\nEquality holds when \\(a = b = c = d\\). So, if we set \\(a = b = c = d = k\\), then:\n\\[\n(a + b + c + d) \\left( \\frac{1}{a} + \\frac{1}{b} + \\frac{1}{c} + \\frac{1}{d} \\right) = (k + k + k + k) \\left( \\frac{1}{k} + \\frac{1}{k} + \\frac{1}{k} + \\frac{1}{k} \\right) = 4k \\cdot \\frac{4}{k} = 16\n\\]\nThus, the minimum value is indeed 16. We can verify this using Python code to check the value for various positive real numbers \\(a, b, c, d\\).\n\nLet's write the Python code to verify this.\n```python\n# Function to calculate the expression (a + b + c + d) * (1/a + 1/b + 1/c + 1/d)\ndef calculate_expression(a, b, c, d):\n    return (a + b + c + d) * (1/a + 1/b + 1/c + 1/d)\n\n# Test the function with a = b = c = d = 1\na = b = c = d = 1\nresult = calculate_expression(a, b, c, d)\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n16.0\n```\nThe Python code confirms that when \\(a = b = c = d = 1\\), the value of the expression \\((a + b + c + d) \\left( \\frac{1}{a} + \\frac{1}{b} + \\frac{1}{c} + \\frac{1}{d} \\right)\\) is 16. \n\nThus, the minimum value of \\((a + b + c + d) \\left( \\frac{1}{a} + \\frac{1}{b} + \\frac{1}{c} + \\frac{1}{d} \\right)\\) is \\(\\boxed{16}\\).", "To find the minimum value of \\((a + b + c + d) \\left(