pm 1}{-4}.\n\\]\n\nThis gives us two solutions:\n\n\\[\nr = \\frac{-15 + 1}{-4} = \\frac{-14}{-4} = \\frac{7}{2},\n\\]\n\\[\nr = \\frac{-15 - 1}{-4} = \\frac{-16}{-4} = 4.\n\\]\n\nHowever, we need to check if these solutions are valid by ensuring that they do not make the denominator \\( 2r - 7 \\) equal to zero. If \\( r = \\frac{7}{2} \\), then \\( 2r - 7 = 2 \\cdot \\frac{7}{2} - 7 = 7 - 7 = 0 \\), so \\( r = \\frac{7}{2} \\) is not a valid solution. If \\( r = 4 \\), then \\( 2r - 7 = 2 \\cdot 4 - 7 = 8 - 7 = 1 \\neq 0 \\), so \\( r = 4 \\) is a valid solution.\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( r \\) is \\( \\boxed{4} \\).", "To solve the equation \\(\\frac{6r^2 - 19r - 7}{2r - 7} = 4r - 3\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Multiply both sides of the equation by \\(2r - 7\\) to eliminate the denominator.\n2. Simplify the resulting equation.\n3. Solve for \\(r\\).\n\nLet's go through the steps:\n\n1. Start with the equation:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{6r^2 - 19r - 7}{2r - 7} = 4r - 3\n   \\]\n   Multiply both sides by \\(2r - 7\\):\n   \\[\n   6r^2 - 19r - 7 = (4r - 3)(2r - 7)\n   \\]\n\n2. Expand the right-hand side:\n   \\[\n   6r^2 - 19r - 7 = 8r^2 - 28r - 6r + 21\n   \\]\n   Simplify the right-hand side:\n   \\[\n   6r^2 - 19r - 7 = 8r^2 - 34r + 21\n   \\]\n\n3. Move all terms to one side of the equation to set it to zero:\n   \\[\n   6r^2 - 19r - 7 - 8r^2 + 34r - 21 = 0\n   \\]\n   Combine like terms:\n   \\[\n   -2r^2 + 15r - 28 = 0\n   \\]\n   Multiply through by -1 to make the leading coefficient positive:\n   \\[\n   2r^2 - 15r + 28 = 0\n   \\]\n\n4. Solve the quadratic equation \\(2r^2 - 15r + 28 = 0\\) using the quadratic formula \\(r = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\\), where \\(a = 2\\), \\(b = -15\\), and \\(c = 28\\).\n\nLet's calculate the solutions using Python.\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Coefficients of the quadratic equation\na = 2\nb = -15\nc = 28\n\n# Using sympy to solve the quadratic equation\nr = sp.symbols('r')\nsolutions = sp.solv