.\n\nLet's confirm this with a Python code snippet using sympy to illustrate the reasoning.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Number of circles\nn = 4\n\n# Each pair of circles can intersect at most at 2 points\nmax_intersections = sp.binomial(n, 2) * 2\n\nprint(max_intersections)\n```\n```output\n12\n```\nThe maximum number of points where at least two of the four distinct circles can intersect is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).\n\nNext, we need to determine which of the given volumes could be the volume of a rectangular box with integer side lengths in the ratio \\(1:3:4\\). Let the side lengths be \\(x\\), \\(3x\\), and \\(4x\\). The volume \\(V\\) of the box is given by:\n\\[ V = x \\cdot 3x \\cdot 4x = 12x^3 \\]\n\nWe need to check which of the given volumes (36, 72, 108, 144, 180) can be expressed as \\(12x^3\\) for some integer \\(x\\).\n\nLet's check each volume one by one.\n\n1. For \\(V = 36\\):\n\\[ 12x^3 = 36 \\implies x^3 = 3 \\]\nSince 3 is not a perfect cube, \\(x\\) is not an integer.\n\n2. For \\(V = 72\\):\n\\[ 12x^3 = 72 \\implies x^3 = 6 \\]\nSince 6 is not a perfect cube, \\(x\\) is not an integer.\n\n3. For \\(V = 108\\):\n\\[ 12x^3 = 108 \\implies x^3 = 9 \\]\nSince 9 is not a perfect cube, \\(x\\) is not an integer.\n\n4. For \\(V = 144\\):\n\\[ 12x^3 = 144 \\implies x^3 = 12 \\]\nSince 12 is not a perfect cube, \\(x\\) is not an integer.\n\n5. For \\(V = 180\\):\n\\[ 12x^3 = 180 \\implies x^3 = 15 \\]\nSince 15 is not a perfect cube, \\(x\\) is not an integer.\n\nNone of the given volumes can be expressed as \\(12x^3\\) for some integer \\(x\\). Therefore, none of the given volumes could be the volume of the box.\n\nThe final answer is that none of the given volumes (36, 72, 108, 144, 180) could be the volume of the box.", "Five distinct lines are drawn in a plane. What is the maximum number of points where at least two of the lines intersect? \\boxed{}. Shay\n Four distinct circles are drawn in a plane. Each pair of circles can intersect at most at 