\) and then compute the result modulo 9. We can simplify our calculations by using the property that a number is congruent modulo 9 to the sum of its digits. This property allows us to find the sum of the digits of each number in the series and then sum those values, which will give us the same result as summing the original series and then taking modulo 9.\n\nLet's break down the steps:\n\n1. Find the sum of the digits for each number in the series.\n2. Sum these digit sums.\n3. Compute the result modulo 9.\n\nLet's do this step-by-step using Python code.\n```python\n# Define the series\nseries = [1, 12, 123, 1234, 12345, 123456, 1234567, 12345678]\n\n# Calculate the sum of the digits for each number in the series\ndigit_sums = [sum(int(digit) for digit in str(number)) for number in series]\n\n# Sum the digit sums\ntotal_sum_of_digits = sum(digit_sums)\n\n# Compute the result modulo 9\nresult = total_sum_of_digits % 9\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n6\n```\nThe value of \\( n \\) that satisfies the given condition is \\( \\boxed{6} \\).", "To solve the inequality \\(\\frac{1}{x - 5} > 0\\), we need to determine the values of \\(x\\) for which the expression \\(\\frac{1}{x - 5}\\) is positive. \n\nHere are the steps to solve the inequality:\n\n1. Identify the critical points where the expression \\(\\frac{1}{x - 5}\\) changes sign or is undefined.\n2. Determine the intervals based on these critical points.\n3. Test the sign of the expression in each interval.\n4. Identify the intervals where the expression is positive.\n\nLet's solve this step-by-step using Python and sympy.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable\nx = sp.symbols('x')\n\n# Define the inequality\ninequality = 1 / (x - 5) > 0\n\n# Solve the inequality\nsolution = sp.solve_univariate_inequality(inequality, x, relational=False)\n\n# Print the solution\nprint(solution)\n```\n```output\nInterval.open(5, oo)\n```\nThe solution to the inequality \\(\\frac{1}{x - 5} > 0\\) is \\(x \\in (5, 