lue expression:\n\\[ |x-4| = 12 \\]\n\nThis absolute value equation has two cases:\n1. $x-4 = 12$\n2. $x-4 = -12$\n\nLet's solve each case separately.\n\nFor the first case:\n\\[ x-4 = 12 \\]\n\\[ x = 12 + 4 \\]\n\\[ x = 16 \\]\n\nFor the second case:\n\\[ x-4 = -12 \\]\n\\[ x = -12 + 4 \\]\n\\[ x = -8 \\]\n\nSo, the two possible values of $x$ are 16 and -8. The product of these values is:\n\\[ 16 \\times (-8) = -128 \\]\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure the accuracy of our solution.\n```python\n# Define the two possible values of x\nx1 = 16\nx2 = -8\n\n# Calculate the product of the two possible values of x\nproduct = x1 * x2\nprint(product)\n```\n```output\n-128\n```\nThe product of all possible values of $x$ is \\(\\boxed{-128}\\).", 'In the equation $|x-5| + 7 = 10$, what is the product of all possible values of $x$?', "To solve the equation $|x-4| - 10 = 2$, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Isolate the absolute value expression.\n2. Solve the resulting equations without the absolute value.\n3. Find the product of all possible values of $x$.\n\nLet's start by isolating the absolute value expression:\n\n\\[ |x-4| - 10 = 2 \\]\n\\[ |x-4| = 12 \\]\n\nThe absolute value equation $|x-4| = 12$ means that $x-4 = 12$ or $x-4 = -12$. We can solve these two equations separately:\n\n1. $x - 4 = 12$\n2. $x - 4 = -12$\n\nLet's solve these equations using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Solving the equations x - 4 = 12 and x - 4 = -12\nsolution1 = 12 + 4\nsolution2 = -12 + 4\n\n# The solutions are\nsolutions = [solution1, solution2]\nprint(solutions)\n```\n```output\n[16, -8]\n```\nThe solutions to the equation $|x-4| - 10 = 2$ are $x = 16$ and $x = -8$. \n\nNow, we need to find the product of these solutions:\n\n\\[ 16 \\times (-8) = -128 \\]\n\nSo, the product of all possible values of $x$ is \\(\\boxed{-128}\\).", "To solve the equation \\(|x-4| - 10 = 2\\), we first isolate the absolute value term:\n\n\\[|x-4| = 12\\]\n\nThe equation \\(|x-4| = 12\\