s:**\n   - The shaded region consists of two parts: a segment of the larger circle and a segment of the smaller circle.\n   - The area of the segment of the larger circle is the area of the sector minus the area of the triangle.\n   - The area of the segment of the smaller circle is similarly the area of the sector minus the area of the triangle.\n\n4. **Set Up the Equations:**\n   - Let \\(\\theta\\) be the angle \\(\\angle ADC\\) in radians.\n   - The area of the sector of the larger circle is \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2^2 \\cdot \\theta = 2\\theta\\).\n   - The area of the triangle of the larger circle is \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot \\sin(\\theta) = 2\\sin(\\theta)\\).\n   - So the area of the segment of the larger circle is \\(2\\theta - 2\\sin(\\theta)\\).\n   - The area of the sector of the smaller circle is \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 1^2 \\cdot \\theta = \\frac{\\theta}{2}\\).\n   - The area of the triangle of the smaller circle is \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 1 \\cdot 1 \\cdot \\sin(\\theta) = \\frac{\\sin(\\theta)}{2}\\).\n   - So the area of the segment of the smaller circle is \\(\\frac{\\theta}{2} - \\frac{\\sin(\\theta)}{2}\\).\n   - The total shaded area is \\(2\\theta - 2\\sin(\\theta) + \\frac{\\theta}{2} - \\frac{\\sin(\\theta)}{2} = \\frac{5\\theta}{2} - \\frac{5\\sin(\\theta)}{2} = \\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\).\n\n5. **Solve for \\(\\theta\\):**\n   - We need to solve the equation \\(\\frac{5\\theta}{2} - \\frac{5\\sin(\\theta)}{2} = \\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\).\n\nLet's implement this in Python using sympy to solve for \\(\\theta\\).\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable\ntheta = sp.symbols('theta')\n\n# Define the equation\nequation = sp.Eq((5 * theta / 2) - (5 * sp.sin(theta) / 2), 5 * sp.pi / 3)\n\n# Solve the equation for theta\nsolution = sp.solve(equation, theta)\n\n# Convert the solution from radians to degrees\nangle_degrees = [sp.deg(sol.evalf()) for sol in solution if sol.evalf() > 0 and sol.evalf() < sp.pi]\n\n# Print the solution\n