 its floor will be 0. Therefore, the distinct values in the range of \\( f(x) \\) are \\( \\{1, -1, 0\\} \\).\n\nLet's write the Python code to confirm this:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the function\ndef f(x):\n    return sp.floor((-5/8)**x)\n\n# Evaluate the function for the first few integer values of x\nvalues = set()\nfor x in range(10):  # We can check the first 10 values to confirm the pattern\n    values.add(f(x))\n\n# Print the distinct values\nprint(values)\nprint(len(values))\n```\n```output\n{0, 1, -1}\n3\n```\nThe distinct values in the range of the function \\( f(x) = \\left\\lfloor \\left( -\\frac{5}{8} \\right)^x \\right\\rfloor \\) are \\(\\{1, -1, 0\\}\\). Therefore, the number of distinct values in the range of \\( f(x) \\) is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to analyze the function \\( f(x) = \\left\\lfloor \\left( -\\frac{5}{8} \\right)^x \\right\\rfloor \\) for \\( x \\in [0, \\infty) \\).\n\n1. **Understand the behavior of the function:**\n   - For \\( x = 0 \\), \\( \\left( -\\frac{5}{8} \\right)^0 = 1 \\), so \\( f(0) = \\left\\lfloor 1 \\right\\rfloor = 1 \\).\n   - For \\( x > 0 \\), \\( \\left( -\\frac{5}{8} \\right)^x \\) is a negative number if \\( x \\) is odd and a positive number if \\( x \\) is even. However, as \\( x \\) increases, \\( \\left| \\left( -\\frac{5}{8} \\right)^x \\right| \\) decreases and approaches 0. Therefore, for large \\( x \\), \\( \\left( -\\frac{5}{8} \\right)^x \\) will be a very small negative number, and \\( f(x) = \\left\\lfloor \\left( -\\frac{5}{8} \\right)^x \\right\\rfloor = -1 \\).\n\n2. **Determine the distinct values in the range of \\( f(x) \\):**\n   - For \\( x = 0 \\), \\( f(x) = 1 \\).\n   - For \\( x > 0 \\), \\( f(x) = -1 \\) for all \\( x \\) such that \\( \\left( -\\frac{5}{8} \\right)^x \\) is a negative number close to 0.\n\nTherefore, the function \\( f(x) \\) can only take two distinct values: 1 and -1.\n\nThe number of distinct values in the range of \