re picked from the box at random, what is the probability that both of them are milk chocolate? Shaynuser Shaynuser\nA card is drawn at random from a standard deck of cards. What is the probability of drawing a red card? Shaynuser Shaynuser\nIf a coin is flipped 3 times, what is the probability of getting exactly 2 heads? Shaynuser Shaynuser\nA bag contains 10 balls numbered from 1 to 10. If 3 balls are drawn from the bag at random without replacement, what is the probability that all 3 balls have odd numbers? Shaynuser Shaynuser\nA spinner has 8 equal sections numbered 1 through 8. If the spinner is spun once, what is the probability that it lands on a number greater than 5? Shaynuser Shaynuser\nIf a die is rolled twice, what is the probability of getting a sum of 7? Shaynuser Shaynuser\nA bag contains 5 red balls, 4 blue balls, and 3 green balls. If 2 balls are drawn from the bag at random without replacement, what is the probability that both balls are the same color? Shaynuser Shaynuser\nA coin is flipped 5 times. What is the probability of getting at least 3 heads? Shaynuser Shaynuser\nA box contains 10 balls numbered from 1 to 10. If 2 balls are drawn from the box at random without replacement, what is the probability that the sum of the numbers on the balls is even? Shaynuser Shaynuser\nA bag contains 12 red marbles, 8 blue marbles, and 10 green marbles. If 3 marbles are drawn from the bag at random without replacement, what is the probability that all 3 marbles are the same color? Shaynuser Shaynuser\nA spinner has 10 equal sections numbered 1 through 10. If the spinner is spun once, what is the probability that it lands on a number that is a multiple of 3? Shaynuser Shaynuser\nIf a die is rolled twice, what is the probability of getting a sum of 10? Shaynuser Shaynuser\nA bag contains 6 red balls, 5 blue balls, and 4 green balls. If 2 balls are drawn from the bag at random without replacement, what is the probability that both balls are different colors? Sh