 Rulz}\n\nAssistant: To find the units digit of a number, we only need to consider the units digit of the base number and how it behaves when raised to a power. Here's the step-by-step approach for each problem:\n\n1. **Find the units digit of \\(18^6\\):**\n   - The units digit of 18 is 8.\n   - We need to find the units digit of \\(8^6\\).\n   - Observe the pattern in the units digits of the powers of 8:\n     \\[\n     \\begin{align*}\n     8^1 & = 8 \\quad (\\text{units digit is } 8) \\\\\n     8^2 & = 64 \\quad (\\text{units digit is } 4) \\\\\n     8^3 & = 512 \\quad (\\text{units digit is } 2) \\\\\n     8^4 & = 4096 \\quad (\\text{units digit is } 6) \\\\\n     8^5 & = 32768 \\quad (\\text{units digit is } 8) \\\\\n     8^6 & = 262144 \\quad (\\text{units digit is } 4) \\\\\n     \\end{align*}\n     \\]\n   - The units digit of \\(8^6\\) is 4.\n\n2. **Find the units digit of \\(17^{19}\\):**\n   - The units digit of 17 is 7.\n   - We need to find the units digit of \\(7^{19}\\).\n   - Observe the pattern in the units digits of the powers of 7:\n     \\[\n     \\begin{align*}\n     7^1 & = 7 \\quad (\\text{units digit is } 7) \\\\\n     7^2 & = 49 \\quad (\\text{units digit is } 9) \\\\\n     7^3 & = 343 \\quad (\\text{units digit is } 3) \\\\\n     7^4 & = 2401 \\quad (\\text{units digit is } 1) \\\\\n     7^5 & = 16807 \\quad (\\text{units digit is } 7) \\\\\n     \\end{align*}\n     \\]\n   - The units digits repeat every 4 numbers: 7, 9, 3, 1.\n   - To find the units digit of \\(7^{19}\\), we need to determine the remainder when 19 is divided by 4:\n     \\[\n     19 \\div 4 = 4 \\text{ remainder } 3\n     \\]\n   - So, the units digit of \\(7^{19}\\) is the same as the units digit of \\(7^3\\), which is 3.\n\nLet's confirm these results using Python code.\n```python\n# Function to find the units digit of a^b\r\ndef units_digit(a, b):\r\n    # Get the units digit of the base\r\n    units_digit_base = a % 10\r\n    # Find the units digit of the power\r\n  