ts digit of \\(2^{12}\\).\n\nLet's solve both parts step-by-step using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Function to find the units digit of a^b\r\ndef units_digit(a, b):\r\n    # Extract the units digit of the base\r\n    units_digit_base = a % 10\r\n    # Calculate the units digit of (units_digit_base ^ b) % 10\r\n    units_digit_result = (units_digit_base ** b) % 10\r\n    return units_digit_result\r\n\r\n# Find the units digit of 18^6\r\nunits_digit_18_6 = units_digit(18, 6)\r\n\r\n# Find the units digit of 12^12\r\nunits_digit_12_12 = units_digit(12, 12)\r\n\r\nprint((units_digit_18_6, units_digit_12_12))\n```\n```output\n(4, 6)\n```\nThe units digit of \\(18^6\\) is \\(\\boxed{4}\\), and the units digit of \\(12^{12}\\) is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).", "Find the units digit of $27^2.$ 1. $21^3$ (1 point)\n2. $35^2$ (1 point)\n3. $18^6$ (2 points)\n4. $27^2$ (2 points)\n5. $13^{13}$ (3 points)\n6. $12^{12}$ (3 points)\n7. $2013^{2013}$ (5 points)\n8. $3^{12345}$ (5 points)\n9. $4^{12345}$ (5 points)\n10. $5^{12345}$ (5 points)\n11. $6^{12345}$ (5 points)\n12. $7^{12345}$ (5 points)\n13. $8^{12345}$ (5 points)\n14. $9^{12345}$ (5 points)\n15. $10^{12345}$ (5 points)\n16. $11^{12345}$ (5 points)\n17. $12^{12345}$ (5 points)\n18. $13^{12345}$ (5 points)\n19. $14^{12345}$ (5 points)\n20. $15^{12345}$ (5 points)\n21. $16^{12345}$ (5 points)\n22. $17^{12345}$ (5 points)\n23. $18^{12345}$ (5 points)\n24. $19^{12345}$ (5 points)\n25. $20^{12345}$ (5 points)\n26. $21^{12345}$ (5 points)\n27. $22^{12345}$ (5 points)\n28. $23^{12345}$ (5 points)\n29. $24^{12345}$ (5 points)\n30. $25^{12345}$ (5 points)\n\nAssistant: To find the units digit of a number raised to a power, we can focus on the units digit of the base number and how it behaves when raised to successive powers. This approach simplifies the problem significantly, as we only need to consider the units digits and their patterns.\n\nLet's solve the problem step-by-step using Python to ensure accuracy.\n\n1. Identify t