thon and SymPy to find the solution.\n\n1. **Understand the Geometry:**\n   - Triangle \\(ABC\\) is isosceles with \\(AB = AC\\) and altitude \\(AM = 11\\).\n   - Point \\(D\\) is on \\(AM\\) such that \\(AD = 10\\), so \\(DM = 1\\).\n   - \\(\\angle BDC = 3 \\angle BAC\\).\n\n2. **Set Up the Coordinates:**\n   - Place \\(A\\) at \\((0, 11)\\), \\(M\\) at \\((0, 0)\\), and \\(B\\) and \\(C\\) at \\((-x, 0)\\) and \\((x, 0)\\) respectively.\n   - Since \\(D\\) is on \\(AM\\), its coordinates are \\((0, 1)\\).\n\n3. **Use Trigonometry:**\n   - Let \\(\\angle BAC = \\theta\\), so \\(\\angle BDC = 3\\theta\\).\n   - The coordinates of \\(B\\) and \\(C\\) are \\((-x, 0)\\) and \\((x, 0)\\) respectively.\n   - The slope of \\(BD\\) is \\(\\frac{1 - 0}{0 - (-x)} = \\frac{1}{x}\\), so \\(\\tan(\\angle BDA) = \\frac{1}{x}\\).\n   - The slope of \\(CD\\) is \\(\\frac{1 - 0}{0 - x} = -\\frac{1}{x}\\), so \\(\\tan(\\angle CDA) = -\\frac{1}{x}\\).\n   - Since \\(\\angle BDC = \\angle BDA + \\angle CDA\\), we can use the tangent addition formula:\n     \\[\n     \\tan(3\\theta) = \\frac{\\tan(\\angle BDA) + \\tan(\\angle CDA)}{1 - \\tan(\\angle BDA)\\tan(\\angle CDA)} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{x} - \\frac{1}{x}}{1 - \\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\left(-\\frac{1}{x}\\right)} = \\frac{0}{1 + \\frac{1}{x^2}} = 0.\n     \\]\n   - This implies that \\(\\angle BDC = 3\\theta = 180^\\circ - 2\\theta\\), so \\(\\theta = 36^\\circ\\).\n\n4. **Find the Length of \\(BC\\):**\n   - Since \\(\\angle BAC = 36^\\circ\\), the base angles of the isosceles triangle are each \\(72^\\circ\\).\n   - Using the Law of Sines in \\(\\triangle ABC\\):\n     \\[\n     \\frac{BC}{\\sin(36^\\circ)} = \\frac{AB}{\\sin(72^\\circ)}.\n     \\]\n   - Since \\(AB = \\sqrt{x^2 + 11^2}\\), we can find \\(x\\) using the fact that \\(\\tan(72^\\circ) = \\frac{11}{x}\\), so \\(x = \\frac{11}{\\tan(72^\\circ)}\\).\n   - The perimeter of \\(\\triangle ABC\\) is \\(2AB + BC\\).\n\nLet's implement this in Python using SymPy:\n\n```