is given by the formula $V = \\text{length} \\times \\text{width} \\times \\text{height}$.\n   - First, we convert the mixed numbers to improper fractions:\n     - Length = $6\\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{13}{2}$\n     - Width = $3\\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{13}{4}$\n     - Height = $4\\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{13}{3}$\n   - The volume is then calculated as:\n     \\[\n     V = \\frac{13}{2} \\times \\frac{13}{4} \\times \\frac{13}{3} = \\frac{13 \\times 13 \\times 13}{2 \\times 4 \\times 3} = \\frac{2197}{24}\n     \\]\n   - Converting $\\frac{2197}{24}$ to a mixed number, we get $91\\frac{13}{24}$.\n\nNow, let's implement this in Python using sympy to confirm our results.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Part 1: Probability that both Dan and Freddie win\nprob_dan_wins = sp.Rational(1, 2)\nprob_freddie_wins = sp.Rational(1, 2)\nprob_both_win = prob_dan_wins * prob_freddie_wins\n\n# Part 2: Volume of the right rectangular prism\nlength = sp.Rational(13, 2)\nwidth = sp.Rational(13, 4)\nheight = sp.Rational(13, 3)\nvolume = length * width * height\n\n# Convert volume to a mixed number\nmixed_volume = sp.Integer(volume // 1) + sp.Rational(volume % 1)\n\nprint(prob_both_win)\nprint(mixed_volume)\n```\n```output\n1/4\n2197/24\n```\nThe output confirms our reasoning. Let's summarize the final answers:\n\n1. The probability that both Dan and Freddie win is $\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}$.\n2. The volume of the right rectangular prism is $\\boxed{91\\frac{13}{24}}$ cubic inches.", 'A right circular cone has base radius 1 cm and height 3 cm. If the height of the cone is tripled, what is the number of cubic centimeters in the new volume of the cone? Express your answer in terms of $\\pi$. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxed{}. \\boxe