[ a^2 + b^2 = c^2 \\]\nwhere \\( a = 21 \\), \\( c = 29 \\), and \\( b \\) is the unknown leg.\n3. Substituting the known values:\n\\[ 21^2 + b^2 = 29^2 \\]\n\\[ 441 + b^2 = 841 \\]\n\\[ b^2 = 841 - 441 \\]\n\\[ b^2 = 400 \\]\n\\[ b = \\sqrt{400} \\]\n\\[ b = 20 \\]\n4. Now that we have both legs of the right triangle (21 inches and 20 inches), we can find the area using the formula for the area of a right triangle:\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{leg}_1 \\times \\text{leg}_2 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 21 \\times 20 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 420 \\]\n\\[ \\text{Area} = 210 \\]\n\nLet's confirm these calculations using Python.\n```python\n# Problem 1: Probability that both Dan and Freddie win\nprob_dan_wins = 1 / 2\nprob_freddie_wins = 1 / 2\nprob_both_win = prob_dan_wins * prob_freddie_wins\n\n# Problem 2: Area of the right triangle\nleg1 = 21\nhypotenuse = 29\nleg2 = (hypotenuse**2 - leg1**2)**0.5\narea_triangle = 0.5 * leg1 * leg2\n\nprint(((prob_both_win, area_triangle)))\n```\n```output\n(0.25, 210.0)\n```\nThe probability that both Dan and Freddie win is \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\).\n\nThe area of the right triangle is \\(210\\) square inches.\n\nSo, the final answers are:\n1. The probability that both Dan and Freddie win is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}\\).\n2. The area of the triangle is \\(\\boxed{210}\\) square inches.", 'A right triangle has side lengths that are consecutive integers. The lengths are 3, 4, and 5 inches. What is the probability that a randomly selected side length is odd? (Express your answer as a fraction.) \\boxed{}. \\quad \\text{Solution:} \\quad \\boxed{\\frac{2}{3}} \\quad \\text{Explanation:} \\quad \\text{The triangle has side lengths 3, 4, and 5 inches.} \\quad \\text{Out of these, 3 and 5 are odd.} \\quad \\text{So, the probability is} \\quad \\frac{2}{3} \\quad \\boxed{}. \\quad \\text{Solution:} \\quad \\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}} \\quad \\text{Explanation:} \\quad \\text{There are 4 candidates fo