cy.\n```python\n# Define the lengths of the bases and the height\nbase1 = 5\nbase2 = 9\nheight = 5\n\n# Calculate the area of the trapezoid\narea = 0.5 * (base1 + base2) * height\nprint(area)\n```\n```output\n35.0\n```\nThe area of the trapezoid is \\(\\boxed{35}\\) square centimeters.", "To find the dot product of two vectors, we need to multiply the corresponding components of the vectors and then sum the results. The dot product of two vectors $\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} a_1 \\\\ a_2 \\\\ a_3 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} b_1 \\\\ b_2 \\\\ b_3 \\end{pmatrix}$ is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = a_1 b_1 + a_2 b_2 + a_3 b_3\n\\]\n\nIn this case, the vectors are $\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix}$. So, the dot product is:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = (-2) \\cdot 3 + 0 \\cdot 4 + 7 \\cdot (-5) = -6 + 0 - 35 = -41\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this by calculating it in Python.\n```python\n# Define the vectors\na = [-2, 0, 7]\nb = [3, 4, -5]\n\n# Calculate the dot product\ndot_product = sum(x*y for x, y in zip(a, b))\nprint(dot_product)\n```\n```output\n-41\n```\nThe dot product of the vectors $\\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix}$ is \\(\\boxed{-41}\\).", "To find the dot product of two vectors, we need to multiply the corresponding components of the vectors and then sum those products. Given the vectors $\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix}$, the dot product $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}$ is calculated as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = (-2) \\cdot 3 + 0 \\cdot 4 + 7 \\cdot (-5) = -6 + 0 - 35 = -41\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this calculation using Python.\n```python\n# Define the vectors\na = [-2, 0, 7]\nb = [3, 4, -5]\n\n# Calculate the dot product\