f boxes that contain neither pencils nor pens is:\n\\[ 10 - |A \\cup B| = 10 - 7 = 3 \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Total number of boxes\ntotal_boxes = 10\n\n# Number of boxes containing pencils\nboxes_with_pencils = 5\n\n# Number of boxes containing pens\nboxes_with_pens = 4\n\n# Number of boxes containing both pencils and pens\nboxes_with_both = 2\n\n# Number of boxes containing either pencils or pens (or both)\nboxes_with_either = boxes_with_pencils + boxes_with_pens - boxes_with_both\n\n# Number of boxes containing neither pencils nor pens\nboxes_with_neither = total_boxes - boxes_with_either\nprint(boxes_with_neither)\n```\n```output\n3\n```\nThe number of boxes that contain neither pens nor pencils is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).", "Roslyn has ten boxes. Five of the boxes contain pencils, four of the boxes contain pens, and two of the boxes contain both pens and pencils. To find the number of boxes that contain neither pens nor pencils, we can use the principle of inclusion and exclusion.\n\nLet's define:\n- \\(A\\) as the set of boxes that contain pencils.\n- \\(B\\) as the set of boxes that contain pens.\n- \\(|A|\\) as the number of boxes that contain pencils, which is 5.\n- \\(|B|\\) as the number of boxes that contain pens, which is 4.\n- \\(|A \\cap B|\\) as the number of boxes that contain both pens and pencils, which is 2.\n\nThe number of boxes that contain either pens or pencils (or both) is given by:\n\\[ |A \\cup B| = |A| + |B| - |A \\cap B| = 5 + 4 - 2 = 7 \\]\n\nSince Roslyn has a total of 10 boxes, the number of boxes that contain neither pens nor pencils is:\n\\[ 10 - |A \\cup B| = 10 - 7 = 3 \\]\n\nSo, the number of boxes that contain neither pens nor pencils is \\( \\boxed{3} \\).\n\nLet's verify this with Python code.\n```python\n# Total number of boxes\ntotal_boxes = 10\n\n# Number of boxes containing pencils\nboxes_with_pencils = 5\n\n# Number of boxes containing pens\nboxes_with_pens = 4\n\n# Number of boxes containing bo