ve this quadratic equation for \\(x\\).\n\n2. **Find the Tangent Lines:**\n\n   The tangent lines to the circle at the points of intersection will be perpendicular to the radius at those points. The tangent lines to the parabola at the points of intersection will have the form \\(y = mx + c\\), where \\(m\\) is the derivative of the parabola at the point of tangency.\n\n3. **Find the Points of Tangency:**\n\n   The points of tangency are the points where the tangent lines to the circle and the parabola intersect. These points will be the solutions to the system of equations formed by the tangent lines.\n\n4. **Calculate the Area of the Quadrilateral:**\n\n   The area of the quadrilateral formed by the four points of tangency can be calculated using the Shoelace formula or by finding the lengths of the sides and using the properties of the quadrilateral.\n\nLet's implement this step-by-step in Python using sympy.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define variables\nx, y = sp.symbols('x y')\n\n# Circle equation: x^2 + y^2 = 2\ncircle_eq = x**2 + y**2 - 2\n\n# Parabola equation: y^2 = 8x\nparabola_eq = y**2 - 8*x\n\n# Solve for points of intersection\nintersection_points = sp.solve([circle_eq, parabola_eq], (x, y))\n\n# Define the derivative of the parabola y^2 = 8x\nparabola_y = sp.sqrt(8*x)\nparabola_y_prime = sp.diff(parabola_y, x)\n\n# Find the slopes of the tangent lines at the points of intersection\ntangent_slopes = [parabola_y_prime.subs(x, point[0]) for point in intersection_points]\n\n# Find the equations of the tangent lines to the parabola\ntangent_lines = [sp.Eq(y, slope*(x - point[0]) + point[1]) for slope, point in zip(tangent_slopes, intersection_points)]\n\n# Find the equations of the tangent lines to the circle\ncircle_center = (0, 0)\ncircle_radius = sp.sqrt(2)\ntangent_lines_circle = [sp.Eq(y, -1/slope*(x - point[0]) + point[1]) for slope, point in zip(tangent_slopes, intersection_points)]\n\n# Find the points of tangency by solving the system of