e matrix $\\mathbf{M}$\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 9 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 7 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nLet $\\mathbf{M} = \\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix}$. Then we have the following system of equations:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n2a - b = 9 \\\\\n2c - d = 3 \\\\\na - 3b = 7 \\\\\nc - 3d = -1\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nWe can solve this system of equations to find the values of $a, b, c,$ and $d$.\n\n### Step 2: Solve the system of equations\n\nLet's solve the system step by step using Python.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\r\n\r\n# Define the variables\r\na, b, c, d = symbols('a b c d')\r\n\r\n# Define the equations\r\neq1 = Eq(2*a - b, 9)\r\neq2 = Eq(2*c - d, 3)\r\neq3 = Eq(a - 3*b, 7)\r\neq4 = Eq(c - 3*d, -1)\r\n\r\n# Solve the system of equations\r\nsolution = solve((eq1, eq2, eq3, eq4), (a, b, c, d))\r\nprint(solution)\n```\n```output\n{a: 23/5, b: 1/5, c: 4/5, d: 7/5}\n```\nThe solution to the system of equations is:\n\\[\na = \\frac{23}{5}, \\quad b = \\frac{1}{5}, \\quad c = \\frac{4}{5}, \\quad d = \\frac{7}{5}\n\\]\nSo the matrix $\\mathbf{M}$ is:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{23}{5} & \\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{7}{5} \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Find the image of the line $y = 2x + 1$ under $\\mathbf{M}$\n\nThe line $y = 2x + 1$ can be parameterized as:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ 2x + 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nWe need to find the image of this line under the transformation $\\mathbf{M}$. Let's apply $\\mathbf{M}$ to the parameterized line:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ 2x + 1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{23}{5} & \\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{7}{5} \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ 2x + 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{23}{5}x + \\frac{1}{5}(2x + 1) 