e \\( \\pi \\approx 3.14159 \\), \\( \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\approx 1.0472 \\). This value is less than 4, so \\( f\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = \\lceil 1.0472 \\rceil = 2 \\).\n\n2. For \\( \\sqrt{45} \\):\n   - \\( \\sqrt{45} \\approx 6.7082 \\). This value is greater than 4, so \\( f(\\sqrt{45}) = \\lfloor 6.7082 \\rfloor = 6 \\).\n\n3. For \\( 8^{2/3} \\):\n   - \\( 8^{2/3} = (2^3)^{2/3} = 2^2 = 4 \\). This value is equal to 4, so \\( f(8^{2/3}) = \\lfloor 4 \\rfloor = 4 \\).\n\nNow we sum these results: \\( f\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right) + f(\\sqrt{45}) + f(8^{2/3}) = 2 + 6 + 4 = 12 \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Define the function f(n)\ndef f(n):\n    if n >= 4:\n        return math.floor(n)\n    else:\n        return math.ceil(n)\n\n# Calculate the values\npi_over_3 = math.pi / 3\nsqrt_45 = math.sqrt(45)\neight_two_thirds = 8 ** (2 / 3)\n\n# Evaluate the function for each value\nresult = f(pi_over_3) + f(sqrt_45) + f(eight_two_thirds)\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n12\n```\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).", "First, let's break down the function \\( f(n) \\):\n\n- If \\( n \\geq 4 \\), then \\( f(n) = \\lfloor n \\rfloor \\).\n- If \\( n < 4 \\), then \\( f(n) = \\lceil n \\rceil \\).\n\nWe need to evaluate \\( f \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\right) \\), \\( f \\left( \\sqrt{45} \\right) \\), and \\( f \\left( 8^{2/3} \\right) \\).\n\n1. Evaluate \\( \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\):\n   - Since \\( \\pi \\approx 3.14159 \\), \\( \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\approx 1.04719 \\). Because \\( 1.04719 < 4 \\), \\( f \\left( \\frac{\\pi}{3} \\right) = \\lceil 1.04719 \\rceil = 2 \\).\n\n2. Evaluate \\( \\sqrt{45} \\):\n   - Since \\( \\sqrt{45} \\approx 6.7082 \\), \\( \\sqrt{45} \\geq 4 \\), so \\( f \\left( \\sqrt{45} \\right) = \\lfloor 6.7082 \\rfloor = 6 \\).\n\n3. Evaluate \\( 8^{2/3} \\):\n   - Since \\( 8^{2/3} = (2^3)^{2/3} = 2^2 = 4 \\), \\( 8^{2/3} = 4 \\). Because \\( 4 \\geq 4 \\), \\( f \\left( 8^{2/3} \\right) = \\lfloor 4 \\rfl