ed number \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) to an improper fraction. The improper fraction equivalent of \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) is:\n\n\\[ 2 \\frac{3}{4} = 2 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{8}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nNow we can substitute the values into the distance formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nTo perform the multiplication, we can multiply 50 by 11 and then divide by 4:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4} \\]\n\nNext, we need to simplify \\(\\frac{550}{4}\\). We can do this by dividing both the numerator and the denominator by their greatest common divisor, which is 2:\n\n\\[ \\frac{550 \\div 2}{4 \\div 2} = \\frac{275}{2} \\]\n\nFinally, we need to convert \\(\\frac{275}{2}\\) to a mixed number. To do this, we divide 275 by 2 to get the whole number part and the remainder will be the numerator of the fractional part:\n\n\\[ 275 \\div 2 = 137 \\text{ remainder } 1 \\]\n\nSo, the mixed number is:\n\n\\[ 137 \\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\nLet\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 11 / 4  # hours (2 3/4 hours)\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_number = int(distance // 1)\nfractional_part = distance % 1\nnumerator = int(fractional_part * 2)  # since the denominator is 2\n\n# Display the result as a mixed number\nmixed_number = f"{whole_number} {numerator}/2" if numerator != 0 else f"{whole_number}"\nprint(mixed_number)\n```\n```output\n137 1/2\n```\nThe distance traveled by the car in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours at a speed of 50 miles per hour is \\(\\boxed{137 \\frac{1}{2}}\\) miles.', 'To solve this problem, we need to calculate the distance traveled by a car moving at a constant speed of 50 miles per hour over a period of \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours. The formula to calculate distance is:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nHere, the speed is 50 miles per hour, and the time is \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours. First, we need to convert the mixed number \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) to an improper fraction. \n\n\\[ 2 \\frac{3}{4} = 2 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{8}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{11}{4} \\]\n\nNow, we can substitute the values into the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = 50 \\times \\frac{11}{4} = \\frac{50 \\times 11}{4} = \\frac{550}{4} \\]\n\nNext, we simplify the fraction \\(\\frac{550}{4}\\) by dividing the numerator and the denominator by their greatest common divisor, which is 2:\n\n\\[ \\frac{550 \\div 2}{4 \\div 2} = \\frac{275}{2} \\]\n\nFinally, we convert the improper fraction \\(\\frac{275}{2}\\) to a mixed number:\n\n\\[ \\frac{275}{2} = 137 \\frac{1}{2} \\]\n\nSo, the car would travel \\(137 \\frac{1}{2}\\) miles in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours. Let\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the speed and time\nspeed = 50  # miles per hour\ntime = 2 + 3/4  # hours\n\n# Calculate the distance\ndistance = speed * time\n\n# Convert the distance to a mixed number\nwhole_part = int(distance)\nfractional_part = distance - whole_part\nfraction_numerator = fractional_part.as_integer_ratio()[0]\nfraction_denominator = fractional_part.as_integer_ratio()[1]\n\n# Simplify the fraction part\nfrom math import gcd\ncommon_divisor = gcd(fraction_numerator, fraction_denominator)\nsimplified_numerator = fraction_numerator // common_divisor\nsimplified_denominator = fraction_denominator // common_divisor\n\n# Display the final distance as a mixed number\nmixed_number = f"{whole_part} {simplified_numerator}/{simplified_denominator}" if simplified_denominator != 1 else f"{whole_part + simplified_numerator / simplified_denominator}"\nprint(mixed_number)\n```\n```output\n137 1/2\n```\nThe car would travel \\(\\boxed{137 \\frac{1}{2}}\\) miles in \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours.', 'To determine how far a car travels at a constant speed of 50 miles per hour for \\(2 \\frac{3}{4}\\) hours, we can use the formula for dis