er } 1 \\]\n\nSo, the mixed number is \\(137\\frac{1}{2}\\).\n\nTherefore, the car would travel \\(\\boxed{137\\frac{1}{2}}\\) miles in \\(2\\frac{3}{4}\\) hours at a speed of 50 miles per hour.", "We are given a magic square where the sum of the numbers in each row, each column, and each of the two main diagonals are equal. We need to find the value of \\( n \\) for the given magic square:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|}\n\\hline\nn-3 & 3 & n+1 \\\\\n\\hline\nn+2 & 2n-9 & 1 \\\\\n\\hline\n2 & n & n-1 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nLet's denote the common sum by \\( S \\). We can set up equations based on the rows, columns, and diagonals.\n\n1. **Sum of the first row:**\n   \\[\n   (n-3) + 3 + (n+1) = S\n   \\]\n\n2. **Sum of the second row:**\n   \\[\n   (n+2) + (2n-9) + 1 = S\n   \\]\n\n3. **Sum of the third row:**\n   \\[\n   2 + n + (n-1) = S\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum of the first column:**\n   \\[\n   (n-3) + (n+2) + 2 = S\n   \\]\n\n5. **Sum of the second column:**\n   \\[\n   3 + (2n-9) + n = S\n   \\]\n\n6. **Sum of the third column:**\n   \\[\n   (n+1) + 1 + (n-1) = S\n   \\]\n\n7. **Sum of the main diagonal (top-left to bottom-right):**\n   \\[\n   (n-3) + (2n-9) + (n-1) = S\n   \\]\n\n8. **Sum of the other diagonal (top-right to bottom-left):**\n   \\[\n   (n+1) + (2n-9) + 2 = S\n   \\]\n\nLet's solve these equations step by step using Python to find the value of \\( n \\).\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\r\n\r\n# Define the variable\r\nn = symbols('n')\r\n\r\n# Define the common sum S\r\nS = symbols('S')\r\n\r\n# Equations based on the magic square properties\r\neq1 = Eq((n-3) + 3 + (n+1), S)\r\neq2 = Eq((n+2) + (2n-9) + 1, S)\r\neq3 = Eq(2 + n + (n-1), S)\r\neq4 = Eq((n-3) + (n+2) + 2, S)\r\neq5 = Eq(3 + (2n-9) + n, S)\r\neq6 = Eq((n+1) + 1 + (n-1), S)\r\neq7 = Eq((n-3) + (2n-9) + (n-1), S)\r\neq8 = Eq((n+1) + (2n-9) + 2, S)\r\n\r\n# Solve the system of equations\r\nsolution = solve((eq1, eq2, eq3, eq4, eq5, eq6, eq7, eq8), (n, S))\r\npr