 set up the equations and solve for \\( S \\) and \\( n \\).\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\n\n# Define the variable\nn = symbols('n')\n\n# Define the common sum S\nS = symbols('S')\n\n# Define the equations for the sums\neq1 = Eq((n-3) + 3 + (n+1), S)\neq2 = Eq((n+2) + (2*n-9) + 1, S)\neq3 = Eq(2 + n + (n-1), S)\neq4 = Eq((n-3) + (n+2) + 2, S)\neq5 = Eq(3 + (2*n-9) + n, S)\neq6 = Eq((n+1) + 1 + (n-1), S)\neq7 = Eq((n-3) + (2*n-9) + (n-1), S)\neq8 = Eq((n+1) + (2*n-9) + 2, S)\n\n# Solve the equations\nsolution = solve((eq1, eq2, eq3, eq4, eq5, eq6, eq7, eq8), (n, S))\nprint(solution)\n```\n```output\n{S: 3*n - 3}\n```\nThe solution to the equations shows that \\( S = 3n - 3 \\). However, we need to find the specific value of \\( n \\) that satisfies all the conditions of the magic square. To do this, we can use the fact that the sum \\( S \\) must be the same for all rows, columns, and diagonals.\n\nLet's use one of the simpler equations to find \\( n \\). We can use the equation from the first row:\n\n\\[ (n-3) + 3 + (n+1) = S \\]\n\\[ n - 3 + 3 + n + 1 = S \\]\n\\[ 2n + 1 = S \\]\n\nSince \\( S = 3n - 3 \\), we can set the two expressions for \\( S \\) equal to each other:\n\n\\[ 2n + 1 = 3n - 3 \\]\n\nSolving for \\( n \\):\n\n\\[ 2n + 1 = 3n - 3 \\]\n\\[ 1 + 3 = 3n - 2n \\]\n\\[ 4 = n \\]\n\nSo, the value of \\( n \\) is \\( 4 \\). Let's verify this by substituting \\( n = 4 \\) back into the magic square and checking the sums of the rows, columns, and diagonals.\n\nThe magic square with \\( n = 4 \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|}\n\\hline\n1 & 3 & 5 \\\\\n\\hline\n6 & -1 & 1 \\\\\n\\hline\n2 & 4 & 3 \\\\\n\\hline\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nLet's check the sums:\n\n1.", "To solve the problem, we need to find the value of \\( n \\) such that the given \\( 3 \\times 3 \\) magic square has equal sums for each row, column, and the two main diagonals. Let's denote the common sum by \\( S \\).\n\nGiven the magic square:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{|c|c|c|}