d the Difference:**\n   - The difference in distance between Martha and Jim is \\(700 - d\\).\n\nLet's implement this in Python using sympy to find the exact difference.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the width and length of the field\nwidth = 300\nlength = 400\n\n# Calculate the diagonal distance Jim walks using the Pythagorean theorem\ndiagonal_distance = sp.sqrt(width**2 + length**2)\n\n# Calculate the distance Martha walks\nmartha_distance = width + length\n\n# Calculate the difference in distance\ndifference = martha_distance - diagonal_distance\n\n# Print the difference\nprint(difference.evalf())\n```\n```output\n100.000000000000\n```\nThe difference in distance between Martha and Jim is \\( \\boxed{100} \\) feet. This means Jim walks 100 feet less than Martha.", 'There are 63 different cards with the numbers 1, 1, 2, 2, ..., 9, 9. How many ways can you choose 2 cards from these 63 cards, such that the numbers on the cards are different and their sum is 10? \\boxed{}. \\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\\quad\